{
  "rationale": "The plant automata separate sensing and motion: G1 models the robot's perception of obstacles, G2 models its motion capabilities. The specifications in E1-E4 enforce safe, progress-oriented exploration: E1 binds clear perception to forward/random_walk, E2-E3 bind obstacle detections to short, directed recovery actions, E4 enforces last-resort full_rotate only after repeated failures. The design ensures the robot spends most time exploring, recovers conservatively, and never chains recovery actions unnecessarily.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate perception and motion into distinct plant automata for modularity.",
    "Specification automata bind perception outcomes to safe, progress-maximizing actions, enforcing conservative recovery and rapid return to exploration."
  ],
